{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T8TTH1GFSvtEAvYNpcbswe","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"a624af22d5816773b91f0c7768daa69617c73c24\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T16:12:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Support authentication failures from the backend (#1918)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b9884006387560e52219b747d953cac9fca2d05f\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T21:38:31+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Suppress Basic auth prompts for paginated REST requests (#1906)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T14:08:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework (#1894)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework\\n\\nRetains a small compatibility shim with the most commonly-used public\\nfunctions now stubbed. These deprecated shims will be removed in a\\nfuture version.\\n\\nThe biggest breaking change is the framework no longer supports rxjs\\ndirectly. Functions that returned Observables now return Promises. A\\nsmall compatibility patch is provided for the notifications system.\\n\\n* Fix `getCurrentUser`'s opts\\n\\n* Remove isLoginEnabled\\n\\n* Sounder re-implementation of getCurrentUser()\\n\\n* Remove more stuff, add back a couple of drop APIs we need, and re-add mocks\\n\\n* More clean-up\\n\\n* Add a changeset gentle-jars-pull.md\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* Clean-up README and _main-content.scss\\n\\n* Fixup changesets\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9dae818f0e30d56c7f31394eda770a3c15c08a8c\",\"date\":\"2026-06-29T22:05:13+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5767: Redirect to Location header URL on session endpoint calls (#1797)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dilan Kavishka\",\"authorEmail\":\"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e16e2d9e16a891670bbf4dd0a79ebe81414405d8\",\"date\":\"2026-05-01T18:32:38+05:30\",\"message\":\"(test) Add regression tests for 401 Location-header redirect in openmrsFetch (#1754)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ash\",\"authorEmail\":\"aishwarya.tripathi2023@vitstudent.ac.in\"},{\"hash\":\"3a27e7c23c9e77c4ee85a5b96f5260160e6e9cb8\",\"date\":\"2025-05-23T13:19:26-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Re-work Framework packages for lighter-weight builds (#1346)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ccb94fb75d78f42247c78aae8445dca611b011f0\",\"date\":\"2024-12-16T16:19:37+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Add some missing test cases and improve typing in test files (#1239)\",\"refs\":\"tag: v6.0.0\",\"body\":\"This PR improves test coverage and standardizes test descriptions across Core. Key changes include:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Adding coverage for missing test cases in the Devtools, Help Menu, and Implementer Tools test suites among others.\\r\\n- Standardizing test case descriptions across all modules.\\r\\n- Improving TypeScript types in test files.\\r\\n- Using `jest.mocked()` instead of direct type assertions for mocks as suggested in our [mocking patterns](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/frontend-modules/unit-and-integration-testing#mocking-patterns) guide.\\r\\n- Adding proper type annotations for mock data and responses\\r\\n- Cleaning up redundant type casts and improving mock implementations\\r\\n- Maintaining consistent naming conventions for mock variables (mock* prefix)\\r\\n- Adding missing type information to test utilities and helpers\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"18368f5b330409ca287d4c41a01ff778578fdfbc\",\"date\":\"2024-01-11T16:16:09+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fea