{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKi2L8QrFaoJBqPdfeJU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Why coverage was added:** PR #1754 added regression tests for the 401 handling in `openmrsFetch`. Its summary says the 401 redirect path had no tests. The PR links to ticket O3-5629.\n\n**What the new tests pin down** (all in `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts`, lines 166-214):\n\n- **401 with a `Location` header** (lines 166-185): `navigate` is called with `{ to: <Location value> }`, so the server's auth-module challenge URL is followed. The test sets `redirectAuthFailure.url` to `''` so the header is the only source.\n- **401 without a `Location` header** (lines 197-214): `navigate` goes to the default login URL, `${openmrsSpaBase}/login`. The test also sets `url` to `''`.\n\nThe wrapper logic these tests exercise is in `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts`, lines 225-243. The target is chosen in this order: the configured `redirectAuthFailure.url`, then the response's `Location` header, then `defaultRedirectAuthFailureUrl` (line 234). The question's wording says the configured page is used only when there is no redirect target. The code actually checks the configured URL first, so the `Location` header only applies when that URL is blank.\n\nTwo other tests in the same file cover nearby behavior. Lines 216-233 check that a configured `url` is used on a 401. Lines 235-243 check `rejectAuthFailure`. I did not confirm which of these were added by #1754 versus earlier, because I only had the PR's file stats (63 additions, 1 deletion) and not its diff.\n\n**Which change and ticket:** the test commit is `e16e2d9e` (\"(test) Add regression tests for 401 Location-header redirect in openmrsFetch (#1754)\"), merged 2026-05-01. The ticket is O3-5629. The related session-endpoint redirect on success (lines 187-195 of `openmrs-fetch.ts`) came from commit `9dae818f` (#1797, O3-5767). That is a different path, so I listed it as supporting evidence only.\n\nI only read the code and history; I did not run the test suite.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 166, \"endLine\": 214},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts\", \"startLine\": 225, \"endLine\": 243},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 216, \"endLine\": 243},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-core\", \"commit\": \"e16e2d9e16a891670bbf4dd0a79ebe81414405d8\"},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-core\", \"pr\": 1754},\n  {\"ticket\": \"O3-5629\"},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts\", \"startLine\": 187, \"endLine\": 195},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-core\", \"commit\": \"9dae818f0e30d56c7f31394eda770a3c15c08a8c\"},\n  {\"ticket\": \"O3-5767\"}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1595,"cache_read_input_tokens":31982,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1595},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d23cbea-3e97-444a-849a-18353bee1faf","uuid":"d1f17bed-b478-42cb-a732-e09586fafb8f","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:18:46.925Z","request_id":"req_011CgKi2KooccZMmRnUEHMnv"}
